                <pb facs="0458" n="378" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg378"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Swenson</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-01-05"><hi rendition="#italic">January 5,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 163.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 286, of the 16th ultimo, inclosing copies of correspondence with Mr. C. Ravn
                    respecting the status of his citizenship.</p>
                <p>Your views on the subject, as expressed in your letter of February 17, 1902, to
                    that gentleman, are commended by the Department.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
